{"id": "unknown-2026-09-10-010", "date": "2026-09-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Can trade walls break China’s 94% grip on synthetic yarn?", "content": "China supplied 94.3 per cent of India’s polyester-yarn imports in January–June 2026, 90.6 per cent of Brazil’s and 88.25 per cent of Pakistan’s.\nThe EU cut China’s targeted polyamide-yarn share to 19.2 per cent, but non-Chinese supply rose only 0.2 per cent.\nReplacing half of Chinese import value would require top alternative suppliers to add 506 per cent in Brazil and 1,219 per cent in India.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/can-trade-walls-break-china-s-94-grip-on-synthetic-yarn--313379-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-10-011", "date": "2026-09-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh para-tariffs double effective border protection: World Bank", "content": "Bangladesh’s border protection averages 15.4 per cent with para-tariffs, versus a 7.0 per cent trade-weighted MFN tariff.\nFootwear, hides and skins and transport equipment among others face the widest gaps, shaping sourcing and pricing.\nThe World Bank urges phased cuts and says full reform would cost 0.83 percentage points of GDP.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-para-tariffs-double-effective-border-protection-world-bank-313375-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-10-012", "date": "2026-09-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton futures rise ahead of WASDE amid supply concerns", "content": "ICE cotton futures ended a five-session slide, with December 2026 settling at 87.28 cents, up 0.98 cent.\nUS crop condition worsened as good/excellent ratings fell to 34 per cent, keeping supply concerns in focus before Friday’s WASDE.\nChina’s State Reserve sold 8,007 tonnes in its 38th sold-out auction, while domestic ZCE cotton stayed weak.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-futures-rise-ahead-of-wasde-amid-supply-concerns-313374-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-10-013", "date": "2026-09-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["loss", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Is polyester's crude-led rally sustainable amid weak demand?", "content": "Global polyester feedstock markets firmed in the first week of September 2026 as US-Iran tensions lifted crude oil, PTA and MEG.\nPTA rose across major routes, with CFR India up 1.6 per cent and CFR Southeast Asia up 2.8 per cent between August 31 and September 4.\nMEG gains were sharper, led by domestic China up 13.5 per cent, but weak downstream demand left polyester makers nursing wider losses.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/is-polyester-s-crude-led-rally-sustainable-amid-weak-demand--313371-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-10-014", "date": "2026-09-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "World Bank urges Bangladesh to cut tariffs ahead of LDC graduation", "content": "World Bank has advised Bangladesh to phase down tariffs, remove para-tariffs and negotiate deeper trade agreements as LDC graduation approaches.\nFor apparel, footwear and input-dependent manufacturers, lower duties could improve sourcing costs but reduce border-tax protection.\nThe study warns abrupt reform could hit import-tax revenue, so fiscal and worker-adjustment measures are needed.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/world-bank-urges-bangladesh-to-cut-tariffs-ahead-of-ldc-graduation-313366-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-10-015", "date": "2026-09-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian minister Goyal urges BRICS push for women-led exporters", "content": "Indian minister Piyush Goyal has urged BRICS to expand opportunities for women-led enterprises in global trade through easier credit, buyer access and predictable rules.\nFor textile and apparel exporters, proposed BRICS platforms, e-documents and sectoral women-led delegations could widen market links.\nGoyal also pushed action on invoice discounting, exhibitions and a Women’s Advancement Fund up to 2030.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indian-minister-goyal-urges-brics-push-for-women-led-exporters-313369-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
